      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "The rule kernel decides from the run's own history and the admitted policy",
        "A denial fails the call before it is scheduled with a witness",
        "an escalation parks a frozen copy of the call until a person with the role answers, through an Update the interceptor installs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "Plan admission and verified principals, which have their own questions",
        "the ledger, which records the outcome but never influences it",
        "Connected but out of scope: Ledger chain, Sealed headers, Temporal server, Verified principals, Plan admission, PolyflowPlugin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Doctrine",
      "items": [
        "A denial carries a witness the agent can re-plan from — the failure names the rules that fired, what would fix each, and the kinds allowed right now; an agent that reads it stops retrying the same call",
        "Undeclared is denied — at guard level an activity the policy does not name is denied unless the policy says otherwise; a routed tool the policy does not name is always denied"
      ]
    }
  ]
